# .nxignore — what eden's project graph must never glob in.
#
# Eden carries `.devcontainer/`, `libs/` and `infrastructure/` as git submodules and builds ONE nx
# graph over the whole checkout. A submodule's TEST FIXTURES are not eden's projects, but a fixture
# realistic enough to be useful looks exactly like one.
#
# WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST. A fixture project file inside a submodule is invisible to BOTH
# repositories' gates: the submodule builds no nx graph, so its own CI never reads the name
# (`.devcontainer`'s `cmd_validate` runs `jq empty` and nothing more); and eden never sees the file
# until its POINTER MOVES. So the first thing in the estate able to observe a collision is a
# submodule pointer bump — the worst possible place. gophersys/eden#14 carried 847 commits and zero
# TypeScript and died at `NX Failed to process project graph`, because `.devcontainer` grew a second
# `first`/`second` fixture pair in `40edaaf`.
#
# THREE FILE TYPES, NOT ONE. `nx.json` enables the `@nx/js/typescript` plugin, so a project is
# inferred from `package.json` + `tsconfig*.json` as well as declared by `project.json`. An earlier
# draft of this file listed `project.json` alone and called the class closed; an adversarial
# refutation planted a fixture with NO `project.json` — a bare `package.json` + `tsconfig.json` —
# and it entered the graph while the gate reported clean. Every pattern below therefore comes in a
# set of three, and the guard derives that same set rather than trusting this comment.
#
# WHY THE PATTERNS END IN A FILE NAME rather than excluding the fixture trees whole. `.nxignore`
# hides a path from nx completely — from project detection AND from the file reads behind
# `nx affected`. Excluding `**/testdata/` whole would stop a change to a Go testdata file from
# marking its library affected, and the gate would quietly stop covering it: the FAIL-NOT-SKIP
# failure, traded in to fix a graph error. Hiding the project-DEFINING files alone removes the
# phantom project and leaves every other fixture file visible to affected. Measured: a `data.txt`
# sitting beside an ignored fixture `project.json` still resolves to its owning project.
#
# EDEN'S OWN TREE IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. A duplicate name eden itself commits is caught by eden's
# own gate on the pull request that adds it. The submodules are the blind spot; eden is not.
#
# THIS FILE HAS A HOLDER: `bash .ci/ctl.sh graph-guard`, run by `on-pr.yml` and `on-push.yml`. It
# does two things this file cannot do for itself. It asserts every pattern below is PRESENT, so
# deleting or mangling this file goes RED even on a tree that currently holds no fixture at all.
# And it judges the graph by project ROOT rather than by name, so a fixture that nx infers through
# any mechanism — present or future — is caught even if no pattern here matches it. The guard's
# directory vocabulary is deliberately WIDER than the list below; an escape is a RED gate, never a
# quiet hole.

# --- .devcontainer ---
.devcontainer/**/fixture/**/project.json
.devcontainer/**/fixture/**/package.json
.devcontainer/**/fixture/**/tsconfig*.json
.devcontainer/**/fixtures/**/project.json
.devcontainer/**/fixtures/**/package.json
.devcontainer/**/fixtures/**/tsconfig*.json
.devcontainer/**/__fixtures__/**/project.json
.devcontainer/**/__fixtures__/**/package.json
.devcontainer/**/__fixtures__/**/tsconfig*.json
.devcontainer/**/testdata/**/project.json
.devcontainer/**/testdata/**/package.json
.devcontainer/**/testdata/**/tsconfig*.json

# --- libs ---
libs/**/fixture/**/project.json
libs/**/fixture/**/package.json
libs/**/fixture/**/tsconfig*.json
libs/**/fixtures/**/project.json
libs/**/fixtures/**/package.json
libs/**/fixtures/**/tsconfig*.json
libs/**/__fixtures__/**/project.json
libs/**/__fixtures__/**/package.json
libs/**/__fixtures__/**/tsconfig*.json
libs/**/testdata/**/project.json
libs/**/testdata/**/package.json
libs/**/testdata/**/tsconfig*.json

# --- infrastructure ---
infrastructure/**/fixture/**/project.json
infrastructure/**/fixture/**/package.json
infrastructure/**/fixture/**/tsconfig*.json
infrastructure/**/fixtures/**/project.json
infrastructure/**/fixtures/**/package.json
infrastructure/**/fixtures/**/tsconfig*.json
infrastructure/**/__fixtures__/**/project.json
infrastructure/**/__fixtures__/**/package.json
infrastructure/**/__fixtures__/**/tsconfig*.json
infrastructure/**/testdata/**/project.json
infrastructure/**/testdata/**/package.json
infrastructure/**/testdata/**/tsconfig*.json

